<mujoco model="g1 mixed terrain">
  <include file="g1_29dof_mode_15_unitree_model_collision.xml"/>

  <!--
    Five original parallel lanes traversed along +X, each 2 m wide with 1 m gaps:
      stairs: Y=+3 m; slopes: Y=0 m; climbing platforms: Y=-3 m.
      stones: Y=+6 m; gap: Y=-6 m; both centred at X=10.3 m.
    Stones use four staggered columns and eight rows, with 1.50 m landings.
    Gap widths are 0.50 / 0.60 / 0.70 / 0.80 / 0.90 / 1.00 m,
    separated by 1.50 m resting platforms at 0.60 m height.
    The straight stone and gap lanes share the geometry from their standalone scenes,
    including entry and exit stairs, via terrains/stones.xml and terrains/gap.xml.
    The square and circular ring gap rows are at Y=-15 and Y=-25 m,
    with training levels 5 and 9 at X=5.3 and X=15.3 m, respectively.
    The G1 starts at the origin, facing +X, on a shared flat starting area.
    Four difficulty groups have centres at X=4.1, 8.9, 13.7, 18.5 m.
    Each group fits within a 4.2 m envelope, leaving 0.6 m of flat ground.

    Stairs: four rises of 0.08 / 0.12 / 0.17 / 0.20 m, 0.30 m treads,
    a 1.20 m top landing, then symmetric descending steps.
    Slopes: 8.36 / 16.07 / 23.22 / 29.68 degrees, 1.50 m horizontal run
    on each side and a 1.20 m top landing. Rotated boxes meet the floor
    and landing exactly at their top edges, with their lower edges buried.
    Platforms: 0.30 / 0.40 / 0.50 / 0.60 m high and 1.50 m long.
    Dimensions follow cross_stairs.xml, cross_slope.xml and climb.xml.
    A small-box row at Y=-9 m shares terrains/climb_boxes.xml with climb.xml:
    40x60 cm tops, 15 / 25 / 35 / 45 cm high at the same four X centres.
    Cycle F7 to show site labels with obstacle dimensions.
  -->
